# DROP A WHOLE PACK IN HERE. This decides what git keeps.
#
# Asset bundles ship the same characters four times over: glTF, FBX, .blend
# sources, Unity/Unreal packages, preview renders, marketing images. A creator
# should not have to navigate to exactly the right subfolder — the ingest walks
# directories recursively and finds the models wherever they are — but every
# byte committed here lives in git history permanently, even if deleted later.
#
# So: copy the whole pack folder in, and this keeps only what
# tools/ingest-characters.mjs can actually read.
#
#   .glb                 self-contained, copied with nothing re-encoded
#   .gltf + .bin + png   packed into one .glb losslessly by packGltf()
#
# FBX is DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED. The ingest supports it, but a bundle that also
# ships glTF carries the FBX as a duplicate — and .blend sources are often
# larger than every model combined. If you have a pack that ships FBX ONLY,
# tell me and I will make an exception for that folder rather than opening the
# door to every bundle's worth of duplicates.

# ignore everything...
*

# ...but descend into directories so nested models are still found
!*/

# ...and keep the formats the ingest reads
!*.glb
!*.gltf
!*.bin

# textures a .gltf references by filename — without these it packs a blank skin
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg

# licence files are small and worth keeping with the assets they cover
!LICENSE*
!License*
!license*

!README.md
!.gitignore
